ng are available"], "rationale": "North Dakota's deep Republican lean makes the GOP nominee a heavy favorite, and with no polls, ratings, or market prices to contradict the fundamentals, the forecast holds at the state's partisan margin. Recent presidential results there have been even more lopsided than the lean implies.", "watch": "A decisive national Democratic wave environment could narrow the margin, though carrying the state would require a shift far beyond recent precedent.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "North Dakota stands among the most Republican states on the presidential map, with a partisan lean of roughly 18 points toward the GOP and recent presidential results running even more lopsided. The 2028 contest is an open race, with the incumbent president term-limited, so neither nominee carries an incumbency advantage. No public general-election polls, expert ratings, or prediction-market prices are available for this race, and neither side's fundraising is on record.\n\nWith no countervailing evidence, the forecast rests on the state's fundamentals: a Republican win by roughly 18 points. A strong national Democratic environment could trim that margin, but the state has stayed comfortably in the Republican column even in favorable Democratic years. A Democratic win here would take a shift well beyond anything in recent precedent.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0273, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0549, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0572, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0505, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0515, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_d